# gitleaks' embedded rule set in v8, so an allowlist-only config silently disables the scan. Verified
# against gitleaks 8.30.1: with a minimal config present, a planted `github-pat` stops being
# reported. An entry here is one finding, keyed to the commit, file, rule and line that produced it,
# and it exempts nothing else - same rules, same files, any other line still fails the job.
#
# Regenerating tests/fixtures/local-inference/*.json with
# tools/capture_local_inference_references.py moves these lines and rewrites their commits, so the
# security job will name the new fingerprints in its log and they belong here. Add a fingerprint only
# for a finding you have confirmed was never a live credential.
#
# The six below are the three occurrences, per captured NRP-only plan, of the plan's field naming
# which provider credential a lane is metered under - it carries the identifier `default__qwen3`,
# the name of a file the launcher generates into the instance runtime directory and mounts into
# model-proxy alone, from the credential table in providers/nrp/provider.toml. That identifier is
# also part of the metering key quoted throughout those plans' own guidance text, so it cannot be
# renamed to dodge the rule. The secret itself never reaches a plan.
#
# Do not spell the matched shape out in this file: a comment here quoting that field and its value
